#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 280 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 the object delays each incoming message by a corresponding
delay time from the @t list and outputs it from the corresponding outlet;
#X text 240 138 if @block is 0 and a new message arrives before the
delay time of the previous one has expired \, the old message is discarded
and the new delay time starts from the current moment;
#X text 240 208 a zero delay time means the message is output on the
next Pd runloop iteration (as soon as possible);
#X text 240 248 note: @t and @block can be set only via the right inlet
or with the [prop.set] object;
#X text 240 288 the object can be used to create rhythmic delays and
canonical patterns \, for example to trigger a series of events with
different delays;
